    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41798" root="ودأ" body-key="w">
    
      2 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ودّأ عليه الأَرْضَ</span></b> , inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَوْدِىْءٌ</span>, <i>He made
the earth even,</i> or <i>plain, over him.</i> (AZ, S, K.)
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَدَّأَتْهُ الأَرْضُ</span> <i>The earth,</i> or <i>the land, hid,</i> or
<i>concealed, him.</i> (TA.) [See also 5.] ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ودّأ</span>,
<i>He,</i> or <i>it, buried.</i> (IAar.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ودّأ بِهِمْ</span>, inf. n.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَوْدِئَةٌ</span>; (S, L;) accord. to the K, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَدَأَ</span>; but this
is incorrect; (TA;) <i>He covered,</i> or <i>overwhelmed,
them with evil,</i> or <i>with ill treatment.</i> (L, K.)

